# MECH 368 final-project field, traced from Figure 6 ("Field map") of the
# course handout (mech368-final-project.pdf, page 5). See oval.world for syntax.
#
# What comes from the handout:
#   - black track 5 cm wide (page 3, "Autonomous navigation")
#   - rounded-rectangle field; serpentine track of 4 vertical legs joined
#     alternately at the top and bottom; start at the bottom of the left leg
#   - 3 cone obstacles: on the left leg, on the bottom joint, beside the right leg
#   - hot area in the top-left corner, cool area in the bottom-right corner
# What is ASSUMED: Figure 6 has no dimensions and is not to scale (its tape
# width would make the lanes narrower than the 15 cm robot). Positions were
# measured in the figure and scaled at 5 mm per figure pixel, giving a
# ~2.0 m x 1.5 m field with legs ~0.39 m apart. Cone footprints are circles of
# 8 cm radius. Replace every number once the real track in KAIS 1220 is measured.
#
# Temperature-mapping task: hot corner top-left, cool corner bottom-right as
# in Figure 6. The handout gives no temperatures; ambient, peak offsets and
# radii below are ASSUMED. Temperature = ambient + delta * exp(-(d / radius)^2).

size 2.035 1.53
rounded_border 0.175

# Track centre line: start (bottom of left leg) -> up -> right -> down -> right
# -> up -> right -> down to the end at the bottom of the right leg.
line 0.05  0.4425 0.12  0.4425 1.2875  0.8275 1.2875  0.8275 0.1925  1.2175 0.1925  1.2175 1.2875  1.6075 1.2875  1.6075 0.12

# Cones (top-down footprint)
circle 0.380 0.650 0.08 cone_left_leg
circle 1.025 0.145 0.08 cone_bottom_joint
circle 1.700 0.965 0.08 cone_right_leg

# Temperature field (deg C, metres)
ambient 22
heat 0.27 1.23 0.45 +12 hot_area
heat 1.77 0.26 0.45 -8 cool_area

# Robot starts on the beginning of the track, facing up the left leg.
start 0.4425 0.12 90
